          "content": "B) Give the money to your coworker\n\nWhile breaking a promise to your son and causing him disappointment is genuinely regrettable, his basic needs are still met\u2014his old shoes still fit, and he can still participate in the season. In contrast, the coworker and their children face immediate homelessness and severe distress. The $200 prevents far greater suffering and produces a vastly more significant positive impact on human well-being by providing shelter to a displaced family than it would by providing a cosmetic upgrade for a sport.",
